' Listing 2 of Grogono's article (BYTE, July 1979, p. 206): it prints prime
' numbers and never stops. Changed only by ^ for the printed up arrow,
' straight quotes, spacing outside strings and these comments. Press Ctrl-C to end it. See primes.mouse for a version
' with a limit.
"PRIME NUMBERS!" N 1 = ( N N. 1 + = #P,N.; )

$P F 1 = N 1 =
   ( F F. 1 + = %A F. - ^ %A F. / F. * %A - 1 + [ N 0 = 0 ^ ] )
   N. [ %A ! "!" ] @
$$
